    {
      "id": "claim_0f1b57ea206645a5951a2c7365b1d555",
      "statement": "When the CA requires client authentication, step ssh certificate sends an x509 identity CSR with the SSH sign request, and for host certificates prepends a host-id UUID as the first URI SAN of the identity CSR: reusing an existing identity certificate's UUID by default, deriving a stable v4 UUID from /etc/machine-id via BLAKE2b-128 with a fixed non-secret key for --host-id machine, or parsing an explicit UUID.",
